Nothing here is edited. The house baseline carries the same two files (baseline/vendor/marked/).

Entry modifications (2026-11-16): marked-core.js is a fork of that build,
not the unchanged reference file described above. It specializes the lexer
and renderer for the default synchronous GFM options, removes extension API
handling, caches bullet regexps, gates tokenizers by their possible initial
characters, and reduces unnecessary masking scans and Unicode allocations.
parse.js and main.ts are the entry's own default-only driver.

Direct scanner rewrite (2026-11-16): grammar.js contains the marked 18.1.3
compatibility grammar, helpers, and adapted leaf recognizers, without the marked
Lexer/Parser pipeline. containers.js adapts marked's list indentation and quote
continuation rules to directly rendered HTML. parse.js implements index-based
HTML emission and deferred reference resolution. The extraction scripts and
profiling variants under validation/ are development-only; variants containing
adapted grammar calls share this notice. The original marked licence and
copyright notices are retained in LICENSE and the generated grammar header.
